{
  "version": "Notebook/1.0",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "# 🌍 Authentication Origin Risk Map\n\nMaps the external source IP (`IPAddress`) of interactive Entra ID sign-ins from `SigninLogs`. Bubble **size** and **color** are driven by a composite `RiskScore`, not by raw volume — so the biggest bubble is the most dangerous origin, not your busiest office.\n\n**The bubble to fear is one with both failures and successes, in a country with no baseline traffic.**\n\n> Enriched with `geo_info_from_ip_address()` (MaxMind GeoLite2), with a fallback to Entra ID's own `LocationDetails` resolution for IPv6 addresses the geo DB cannot resolve. Geo data is approximate — trust `Country`, do not act on `City`."
      },
      "name": "header"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "tr",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "TimeRange",
            "label": "Time range",
            "type": 4,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": {
              "durationMs": 604800000
            },
            "typeSettings": {
              "selectableValues": [
                {
                  "durationMs": 3600000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 14400000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 43200000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 86400000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 604800000
                },
                {
                  "durationMs": 2592000000
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "bl",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "BaselineDays",
            "label": "Baseline history (days)",
            "description": "How far back to look to decide which countries are 'normal' for this tenant. The baseline always excludes the displayed time range, so today's attacker cannot whitelist their own country.",
            "type": 2,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": [],
              "showDefault": false
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n  { \"value\": \"14\",  \"label\": \"14 days\" },\n  { \"value\": \"30\",  \"label\": \"30 days\", \"selected\": true },\n  { \"value\": \"60\",  \"label\": \"60 days\" },\n  { \"value\": \"90\",  \"label\": \"90 days\" }\n]"
          },
          {
            "id": "mv",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "MinAttempts",
            "label": "Min attempts per IP",
            "description": "Suppresses single-event bubbles. Set to 1 in a small or lab tenant.",
            "type": 2,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": [],
              "showDefault": false
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n  { \"value\": \"1\",  \"label\": \"1 (show everything)\", \"selected\": true },\n  { \"value\": \"3\",  \"label\": \"3\" },\n  { \"value\": \"5\",  \"label\": \"5\" },\n  { \"value\": \"10\", \"label\": \"10\" }\n]"
          }
        ],
        "style": "pills",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces"
      },
      "name": "parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## 1️⃣ Sign-in origins — `SigninLogs`\n\nOne bubble per source IP. `ResultType != 0` is **not** treated as a failure — MFA challenges, \"keep me signed in\" interrupts, and password-change prompts are bucketed separately as *Interrupts* so they do not inflate legitimate users' bubbles."
      },
      "name": "text-map"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "// === Authentication Origin Risk Map ===\n// One bubble per source IP: where auth originates, whether it succeeded,\n// and whether that origin is normal for this tenant.\n//\n// Result codes that are NOT security failures - auth interrupts and prompts:\n//   50140 = \"Keep me signed in\" interrupt      50074 = MFA required (challenge issued)\n//   50072 = user must enroll in MFA            50076 = MFA required from new location\n//   50133 = session invalid, password changed  50144 = password expired, must change\nlet benign_interrupts = dynamic([50140, 50074, 50072, 50076, 50133, 50144, 50055]);\n//\n// Start of the displayed window. The baseline stops here so that activity being\n// plotted right now can never contribute to what counts as \"normal\".\nlet WindowStart = toscalar(\n    SigninLogs\n    | where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n    | summarize min(TimeGenerated));\n//\n// Countries this tenant has signed in from SUCCESSFULLY before the window.\n// Successes only - including failures would let an attacker country whitelist itself.\nlet KnownCountries =\n    SigninLogs\n    | where TimeGenerated between (ago({BaselineDays}d) .. WindowStart)\n    | where ResultType == 0\n    | summarize BaselineSuccesses = count() by Country = tostring(Location)\n    | where BaselineSuccesses >= 5;   // stops one traveling exec becoming a permanent exception\n//\nSigninLogs\n| where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n| where isnotempty(IPAddress)\n| where isnotempty(UserPrincipalName)          // drop service principal / non-user rows\n//\n// Three buckets, not the usual success/fail binary.\n| extend Outcome = case(\n    ResultType == 0,                          \"Success\",\n    ResultType in (benign_interrupts),        \"Interrupt\",\n                                              \"Failure\")\n//\n// --- Geo enrichment ---\n| extend geo = geo_info_from_ip_address(IPAddress)\n| extend Latitude  = toreal(geo.latitude),\n         Longitude = toreal(geo.longitude),\n         Country   = tostring(geo.country),\n         State     = tostring(geo.state),\n         City      = tostring(geo.city)\n//\n// Fallback to Entra's own sign-in-time resolution. Critical in IPv6-heavy tenants:\n// without it most rows resolve to null coordinates and vanish from the map.\n| extend loc = todynamic(LocationDetails)\n| extend Latitude  = iff(isnull(Latitude),  toreal(loc.geoCoordinates.latitude),  Latitude),\n         Longitude = iff(isnull(Longitude), toreal(loc.geoCoordinates.longitude), Longitude),\n         Country   = iff(isempty(Country),  tostring(loc.countryOrRegion),        Country),\n         City      = iff(isempty(City),     tostring(loc.city),                   City)\n//\n// No coordinates = nothing to plot. Also removes private/internal addresses.\n| where isnotnull(Latitude) and isnotnull(Longitude)\n| where Latitude != 0 or Longitude != 0\n//\n// --- Aggregate to one row per source IP ---\n| summarize\n        Attempts        = count(),\n        Successes       = countif(Outcome == \"Success\"),\n        Failures        = countif(Outcome == \"Failure\"),\n        Interrupts      = countif(Outcome == \"Interrupt\"),\n        UsersTargeted   = dcount(UserPrincipalName),\n        UsersFailed     = dcountif(UserPrincipalName, Outcome == \"Failure\"),\n        UsersSucceeded  = dcountif(UserPrincipalName, Outcome == \"Success\"),\n        RiskySignIns    = countif(RiskLevelDuringSignIn in (\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\")),\n        FailureCodes    = make_set_if(ResultType, Outcome == \"Failure\", 10),\n        Accounts        = make_set(UserPrincipalName, 20),\n        Apps            = make_set(AppDisplayName, 10),\n        UserAgents      = dcount(UserAgent),\n        ASN             = any(AutonomousSystemNumber),\n        FirstSeen       = min(TimeGenerated),\n        LastSeen        = max(TimeGenerated)\n    by IPAddress, Country, State, City, Latitude, Longitude\n| where Attempts >= {MinAttempts}\n| extend FailureRate = round(100.0 * Failures / Attempts, 1)\n//\n// --- Is this origin normal for the tenant? ---\n| join kind=leftouter KnownCountries on $left.Country == $right.Country\n| extend RareCountry = isnull(BaselineSuccesses)\n| project-away Country1, BaselineSuccesses\n//\n// --- Verdict: first match wins, ordered most severe first ---\n| extend Verdict = case(\n    Failures >= 5 and Successes > 0,                             \"Failed then succeeded - possible compromise\",\n    UsersTargeted >= 5 and Failures >= 10 and FailureRate >= 50, \"Spray / enumeration\",\n    RareCountry and Successes > 0,                               \"Success from unusual country\",\n    RareCountry,                                                 \"Failed auth from unusual country\",\n    RiskySignIns > 0,                                            \"Entra risk detection on this IP\",\n    Failures >= 10,                                              \"High failure volume\",\n                                                                 \"Normal\")\n//\n// Composite score drives bubble SIZE and COLOR, so severity reads visually rather\n// than by attempt count (which would just draw a giant bubble over HQ every time).\n| extend RiskScore =\n        (Failures * 1)\n      + (UsersFailed * 5)                                   // breadth = spray indicator\n      + (iff(Failures >= 5 and Successes > 0, 50, 0))       // the case you must not miss\n      + (iff(RareCountry, 25, 0))\n      + (RiskySignIns * 10)\n//\n| extend MapLabel = strcat(\n        City, \", \", Country, \" | \", IPAddress,\n        \" | \", Successes, \" ok / \", Failures, \" fail across \", UsersTargeted, \" users\",\n        \" | \", Verdict)\n//\n| project Latitude, Longitude, MapLabel, RiskScore, Verdict,\n          IPAddress, Country, State, City, ASN, RareCountry,\n          Attempts, Successes, Failures, Interrupts, FailureRate,\n          UsersTargeted, UsersFailed, UsersSucceeded, RiskySignIns,\n          FailureCodes, Accounts, Apps, UserAgents, FirstSeen, LastSeen\n| order by RiskScore desc, Failures desc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Sign-in origins — bubble size & color = RiskScore",
        "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
        "visualization": "map",
        "mapSettings": {
          "locInfo": "LatLong",
          "latitude": "Latitude",
          "longitude": "Longitude",
          "sizeSettings": "RiskScore",
          "sizeAggregation": "Sum",
          "labelSettings": "MapLabel",
          "legendMetric": "RiskScore",
          "legendAggregation": "Sum",
          "legendColor": "RiskScore",
          "itemColorSettings": {
            "nodeColorField": "RiskScore",
            "colorAggregation": "Sum",
            "type": "heatmap",
            "heatmapPalette": "greenRed"
          }
        }
      },
      "name": "map-signin"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## 2️⃣ Verdict distribution\n\nHow the source IPs break down by pattern. In a healthy tenant this is almost entirely **Normal** — anything else is a work queue."
      },
      "name": "text-verdict"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "let benign_interrupts = dynamic([50140, 50074, 50072, 50076, 50133, 50144, 50055]);\nlet WindowStart = toscalar(\n    SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated {TimeRange} | summarize min(TimeGenerated));\nlet KnownCountries =\n    SigninLogs\n    | where TimeGenerated between (ago({BaselineDays}d) .. WindowStart)\n    | where ResultType == 0\n    | summarize BaselineSuccesses = count() by Country = tostring(Location)\n    | where BaselineSuccesses >= 5;\nSigninLogs\n| where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n| where isnotempty(IPAddress) and isnotempty(UserPrincipalName)\n| extend Outcome = case(ResultType == 0, \"Success\",\n                        ResultType in (benign_interrupts), \"Interrupt\",\n                        \"Failure\")\n| extend Country = tostring(Location)\n| summarize Attempts      = count(),\n            Successes     = countif(Outcome == \"Success\"),\n            Failures      = countif(Outcome == \"Failure\"),\n            UsersTargeted = dcount(UserPrincipalName),\n            UsersFailed   = dcountif(UserPrincipalName, Outcome == \"Failure\"),\n            RiskySignIns  = countif(RiskLevelDuringSignIn in (\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"))\n         by IPAddress, Country\n| where Attempts >= {MinAttempts}\n| extend FailureRate = round(100.0 * Failures / Attempts, 1)\n| join kind=leftouter KnownCountries on $left.Country == $right.Country\n| extend RareCountry = isnull(BaselineSuccesses)\n| extend Verdict = case(\n    Failures >= 5 and Successes > 0,                             \"Failed then succeeded - possible compromise\",\n    UsersTargeted >= 5 and Failures >= 10 and FailureRate >= 50, \"Spray / enumeration\",\n    RareCountry and Successes > 0,                               \"Success from unusual country\",\n    RareCountry,                                                 \"Failed auth from unusual country\",\n    RiskySignIns > 0,                                            \"Entra risk detection on this IP\",\n    Failures >= 10,                                              \"High failure volume\",\n                                                                 \"Normal\")\n| summarize SourceIPs = dcount(IPAddress) by Verdict\n| order by SourceIPs desc",
        "size": 1,
        "title": "Source IPs by verdict",
        "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
        "visualization": "piechart"
      },
      "name": "chart-verdict"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## 3️⃣ Source IP breakdown\n\nSame data as the map, ranked by `RiskScore`, with the accounts and applications touched by each origin. Start at the top row."
      },
      "name": "text-grid"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "// Companion grid: same logic as the map, ranked, with accounts and apps per source.\nlet benign_interrupts = dynamic([50140, 50074, 50072, 50076, 50133, 50144, 50055]);\nlet WindowStart = toscalar(\n    SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated {TimeRange} | summarize min(TimeGenerated));\nlet KnownCountries =\n    SigninLogs\n    | where TimeGenerated between (ago({BaselineDays}d) .. WindowStart)\n    | where ResultType == 0\n    | summarize BaselineSuccesses = count() by Country = tostring(Location)\n    | where BaselineSuccesses >= 5;\nSigninLogs\n| where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n| where isnotempty(IPAddress) and isnotempty(UserPrincipalName)\n| extend Outcome = case(ResultType == 0, \"Success\",\n                        ResultType in (benign_interrupts), \"Interrupt\",\n                        \"Failure\")\n| extend geo = geo_info_from_ip_address(IPAddress)\n| extend loc = todynamic(LocationDetails)\n| extend Country = iff(isempty(tostring(geo.country)), tostring(loc.countryOrRegion), tostring(geo.country)),\n         City    = iff(isempty(tostring(geo.city)),    tostring(loc.city),            tostring(geo.city))\n| summarize Attempts      = count(),\n            Successes     = countif(Outcome == \"Success\"),\n            Failures      = countif(Outcome == \"Failure\"),\n            Interrupts    = countif(Outcome == \"Interrupt\"),\n            UsersTargeted = dcount(UserPrincipalName),\n            UsersFailed   = dcountif(UserPrincipalName, Outcome == \"Failure\"),\n            RiskySignIns  = countif(RiskLevelDuringSignIn in (\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\")),\n            FailureCodes  = make_set_if(ResultType, Outcome == \"Failure\", 10),\n            Accounts      = make_set(UserPrincipalName, 25),\n            Apps          = make_set(AppDisplayName, 10),\n            ASN           = any(AutonomousSystemNumber),\n            LastSeen      = max(TimeGenerated)\n         by IPAddress, Country, City\n| where Attempts >= {MinAttempts}\n| extend FailureRate = round(100.0 * Failures / Attempts, 1)\n| join kind=leftouter KnownCountries on $left.Country == $right.Country\n| extend RareCountry = isnull(BaselineSuccesses)\n| project-away Country1, BaselineSuccesses\n| extend Verdict = case(\n    Failures >= 5 and Successes > 0,                             \"Failed then succeeded - possible compromise\",\n    UsersTargeted >= 5 and Failures >= 10 and FailureRate >= 50, \"Spray / enumeration\",\n    RareCountry and Successes > 0,                               \"Success from unusual country\",\n    RareCountry,                                                 \"Failed auth from unusual country\",\n    RiskySignIns > 0,                                            \"Entra risk detection on this IP\",\n    Failures >= 10,                                              \"High failure volume\",\n                                                                 \"Normal\")\n| extend RiskScore = (Failures * 1) + (UsersFailed * 5)\n                   + iff(Failures >= 5 and Successes > 0, 50, 0)\n                   + iff(RareCountry, 25, 0)\n                   + (RiskySignIns * 10)\n| project RiskScore, Verdict, IPAddress, Country, City, ASN,\n          Attempts, Successes, Failures, Interrupts, FailureRate,\n          UsersTargeted, UsersFailed, RiskySignIns,\n          FailureCodes, Accounts, Apps, LastSeen\n| order by RiskScore desc, Failures desc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Source IP breakdown (ranked by risk)",
        "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "formatters": [
            {
              "columnMatch": "RiskScore",
              "formatter": 8,
              "formatOptions": {
                "palette": "redBright"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Verdict",
              "formatter": 18,
              "formatOptions": {
                "thresholdsOptions": "colors",
                "thresholdsGrid": [
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "Failed then succeeded - possible compromise",
                    "representation": "redBright",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "Spray / enumeration",
                    "representation": "redBright",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "Success from unusual country",
                    "representation": "orange",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "Failed auth from unusual country",
                    "representation": "yellow",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "Entra risk detection on this IP",
                    "representation": "orange",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "==",
                    "thresholdValue": "High failure volume",
                    "representation": "yellow",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  },
                  {
                    "operator": "Default",
                    "thresholdValue": null,
                    "representation": "success",
                    "text": "{0}{1}"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "FailureRate",
              "formatter": 4,
              "formatOptions": {
                "palette": "red"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Failures",
              "formatter": 4,
              "formatOptions": {
                "palette": "red"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Successes",
              "formatter": 4,
              "formatOptions": {
                "palette": "green"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Accounts",
              "formatter": 1
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Apps",
              "formatter": 1
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "FailureCodes",
              "formatter": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "sortBy": []
      },
      "name": "grid-signin"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## 4️⃣ Failure reasons\n\nWhat is actually failing, by Entra result code. `50126` (invalid username or password) rising against many distinct users is the spray signature; `50053` is smart lockout, meaning it has already been going on for a while."
      },
      "name": "text-codes"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "let benign_interrupts = dynamic([50140, 50074, 50072, 50076, 50133, 50144, 50055]);\nSigninLogs\n| where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n| where isnotempty(UserPrincipalName)\n| where ResultType != 0 and ResultType !in (benign_interrupts)\n| summarize Failures    = count(),\n            Users       = dcount(UserPrincipalName),\n            SourceIPs   = dcount(IPAddress),\n            Countries   = make_set(Location, 15)\n         by ResultType = tostring(ResultType),\n            Reason      = ResultDescription\n| order by Failures desc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Failure codes (interrupts and MFA prompts excluded)",
        "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "formatters": [
            {
              "columnMatch": "Failures",
              "formatter": 4,
              "formatOptions": {
                "palette": "red"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Users",
              "formatter": 4,
              "formatOptions": {
                "palette": "orange"
              }
            },
            {
              "columnMatch": "Countries",
              "formatter": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "grid-codes"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "---\n### Reading this dashboard\n\n| Verdict | Action |\n|---|---|\n| **Failed then succeeded** | Treat as compromise until disproven. Revoke sessions, reset credentials, check the AzureActivity map for control-plane follow-on. |\n| **Spray / enumeration** | Confirm smart lockout and Conditional Access are enforcing. Block the ASN if it is not a carrier. |\n| **Success from unusual country** | Verify travel with the user before assuming malice. |\n| **Failed auth from unusual country** | Low urgency on its own; watch for it turning into a success. |\n\n### Caveats\n\n- **Baseline needs history.** With less than `BaselineDays` of data in the workspace, every country flags as rare and the map turns solid red. In a new or lab workspace, replace `KnownCountries` with a hardcoded `datatable` of your expected footprint.\n- **VPN and mobile carriers** produce legitimate rare-country hits. Suppress by `ASN`, not by country — excluding a country creates a real blind spot.\n- **Geo is approximate.** `Country` is reliable enough to act on; `City` is roughly 50-80% accurate for IPv4 and worse for IPv6. Do not put city names in an incident narrative.\n- **Thresholds are starting points.** `UsersTargeted >= 5` and `Failures >= 10` suit a mid-size tenant. Tune to roughly the 95th percentile of your own `UsersFailed` distribution."
      },
      "name": "footer"
    }
  ],
  "fallbackResourceIds": [
    "/subscriptions/3c95e63a-895a-4386-991e-edbbf57de5c8/resourcegroups/cyber-range-admin-soc/providers/microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces/law-cyber-range"
  ],
  "$schema": "https://github.com/Microsoft/Application-Insights-Workbooks/blob/master/schema/workbook.json"
}